---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import DiveInCta from '../components/DiveInCta.astro';
import SpotifyGrid from '../components/SpotifyGrid.astro';
import PlaylistEmbed from '../components/PlaylistEmbed.astro';
import { business as b } from '../data/site';
---
<Base
  title="Lucio Rubino: Producer, Multi-Instrumentalist & Songwriter | The Fish Tank"
  description="Lucio “Lu” Rubino: producer, multi-instrumentalist and programmer. Played on Paramore’s Platinum debut, co-wrote for RED, fronted StorySide:B. The Fish Tank, St. Augustine, FL."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Lucio Rubino', path: '/lucio-rubino/' }]}
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="About · The producer" title="Lucio Rubino: <em>beauty from silence.</em>"
    lede="Singer, songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, programmer and producer, Lucio “Lu” Rubino has spent more than three decades on stages, on other artists’ records and behind the console." />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid split">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Rubino was the first member of his Italian family born in the United States. Born in Connecticut, he moved to St. Augustine in middle school and found his footing in the high school music program, on bass and harmony vocals. His influences ran from early MTV to Peter Gabriel, The Police and Depeche Mode, and later Jeff Buckley.</p>

        <h2>On the road & on the radio</h2>
        <p>His first tour came in <strong>1998, as the touring bassist for A Flock of Seagulls</strong>, the new-wave act behind “I Ran.” Back in Florida, a song he recorded picked up airplay on Jacksonville rock radio and drew label interest, and he signed to <strong>EMI</strong> as a member of Monkey the Fish.</p>
        <p>In 2003 he co-founded <strong>StorySide:B</strong> with drummer Jordan Mohilowski. The band signed to <strong>Gotee Records</strong>, released two albums and placed several songs on Christian radio. Rubino co-wrote “<strong>Be Still</strong>,” which BMI listed among the five most-played songs on Christian radio in 2008.</p>

        <h2>On other people's records</h2>
        <p>While still fronting StorySide:B, Rubino filled in for Paramore’s departed bassist on the Franklin, Tenn., band’s debut, <em>All We Know Is Falling</em>, playing on every track except “Here We Go Again.” The RIAA certified the album <strong>Platinum</strong> in August 2025, and lead single “Pressure” is also Platinum. He co-wrote “<strong>Still Bleeding</strong>,” where he also plays bass, and “<strong>Your Devil Is a Ghost</strong>” for <strong>RED</strong>’s 2023 album <em>Rated R</em>. He produced “<strong>In Time</strong>” on <strong>Grey Daze</strong>’s <em>Amends</em>. Grey Daze was the first band of <strong>Chester Bennington</strong>, who went on to front <strong>Linkin Park</strong>, and <em>Amends</em> rebuilt its songs around Bennington’s original vocals as a tribute after his death. The album reached No. 9 on Billboard’s Top Rock Albums chart.</p>
        <p>He has produced for jazz-fusion guitarist <strong>Larry Coryell</strong>, worked on eight <strong>STARSET</strong> songs and on tracks for <strong>Seventh Day Slumber</strong> and <strong>Manafest</strong>, and written with <strong>Jill Cunniff</strong> of Luscious Jackson. On stage, he has toured Europe with RED and played a show with <strong>Disturbed</strong>. In the Monkey the Fish years, he co-produced the band with Pete Thornton.</p>
        <p>His production credits also include albums for <strong>Manic Drive</strong>, <strong>Todd Lombardo</strong> (the Grammy-nominated guitarist for Jerry Douglas), <strong>Lindsey Dedge</strong> and <strong>Lighthouse Music</strong>. In 2012 he released a self-titled solo album that moves between modern folk, acoustic rock and guitar-driven pop.</p>

        <h2>The Fish Tank</h2>
        <p>Across all of it, Rubino has worked as a true multi-instrumentalist, comfortable on nearly every instrument heard on a modern record, and as a programmer and producer who builds tracks from the ground up.</p>
        <p>Rubino opened The Fish Tank Recordings in {b.founded} as a working creative space rather than a room rented by the hour. The approach has stayed the same since: find what makes a song matter, then make the record that proves it.</p>
        <p><a href="/credits/">Full credits →</a></p>
      </div>
      <aside class="side">
        <img class="img" src="/images/lu-upright-bass.webp" alt="Lucio Rubino playing upright bass on stage" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figure class="plaque"><img class="img" src="/images/paramore-plaque.webp" alt="Framed RIAA plaque for Paramore’s All We Know Is Falling at The Fish Tank" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Paramore’s <em>All We Know Is Falling</em> plaque on the studio wall.</figcaption></figure>
        <ul class="facts">
          <li><span>Plays</span>Vocals · guitars · bass · keys · drums</li>
          <li><span>Studio craft</span>Production · programming · mixing</li>
          <li><span>Performing rights</span>BMI</li>
          <li><span>Labels</span>Gotee · EMI (Monkey the Fish)</li>
          <li><span>Studio since</span>{b.founded}</li>
        </ul>
        <DiveInCta micro={false} label="Book Your Free Dive In Visit" />
        <p class="social"><a href={b.social.instagramLu} target="_blank" rel="noopener">@iamluciorubino ↗</a></p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Listen</p>
      <h2>Rubino <em>on Spotify.</em></h2>
      <SpotifyGrid />
      <div style="margin-top:3rem"><PlaylistEmbed height={380} /></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .side { display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; align-content: start; position: sticky; top: 100px; }
  .plaque { margin: 0; }
  .plaque .img { aspect-ratio: 4/5; }
  .plaque figcaption { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: .5rem; }
  .facts { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .facts li { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: .85rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--cream); font-size: .95rem; }
  .facts span { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .68rem; letter-spacing: .15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .social { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .8rem; }
</style>
